reasoning_over_luck.evidence:
Chance enters only at setup: the type deal and which type goes to nobody.

If everyone plays the intended strategy (owners bid 6 or 8 in their rounds, non-owners mostly stay out), each player banks a similar amount from their own 3 rounds. The winner is then decided by:
- the three value-6 chicken rounds, through escalation reads and talk;
- the owner's 6-versus-8 read;
- early inference of types from rounds 1-4 bids and messages, including bluffing about the unassigned type.

The deal does not decide the result. Timing differences are minor, and I estimate chance at about 15-20% of the outcome. Hidden information exists early and can be acted on: you can contest rounds you believe are unassigned, or bid low against owners you have misread. Opponent modelling of bids and raises persists all game. A reasoning player clearly beats random or passive play: random play totals about -8, passive play scores 0, and sensible play scores 12 or more.
